%I A400743 #10 Oct 06 2026 15:00:41
%S A400743 17,97,193,241,257,353,401,433,449,577,641,673,769,929,977,1009,1153,
%T A400743 1217,1297,1361,1409,1489,1601,1697,1873,1889,2017,2081,2161,2273,
%U A400743 2417,2609,2689,2753,2801,2897,3041,3137,3169,3329,3361,3457,3617,3697,3793,3889,4001
%N A400743 Primes p such that the multiplicative order of 16 modulo p is even.
%C A400743 Primes p such that 1/p has even reptend length in hexadecimal. In other words, prime factors of Phi_{2k}(16) = Phi_{8k}(2) for some k, where Phi_k is the k-th cyclotomic polynomial.
%C A400743 Also primes p such that the multiplicative order of 2 modulo p is divisible by 8.
%C A400743 Also primes p such that the multiplicative order of -2 modulo p is divisible by 8.
%C A400743 All terms are congruent to 1 modulo 16. As a consequence, if p is a term and d is the multiplicative order of 16 modulo p then we always have (16^d - 1)/p == 15 (mod 16) (i.e., the reptend of 1/p always ends with the hexadecimal digit "F").
%H A400743 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400743/b400743.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A400743 17 is a term since the multiplicative order of 16 modulo 17 is 2 (1/17 is 0.(0F) in hexadecimal).
%e A400743 97 is a term since the multiplicative order of 16 modulo 97 is 12 (1/97 is 0.(02A3A0FD5C5F) in hexadecimal).
%e A400743 193 is a term since the multiplicative order of 16 modulo 193 is 24 (1/193 is 0.(015390948F40FEAC6F6B70BF) in hexadecimal).
%e A400743 241 is a term since the multiplicative order of 16 modulo 241 is 6 (1/241 is 0.(010FEF) in hexadecimal).
%o A400743 (PARI) isA400743(p) = isprime(p) && (p>2) && (znorder(Mod(16,p))%2==0)
%Y A400743 Cf. A302141, A105876 (p such that ord(16,p) = (p-1)/2).
%Y A400743 Subsequence of A094407.
%K A400743 nonn,easy,new
%O A400743 1,1
%A A400743 _Jianing Song_, Oct 05 2026
